derivations.claim:
For an arbitrary tangent field $V$ along a curve, the formula in step 2.1 gives $D_t^{
abla}V=V'+\langle\dot\gamma,Vangle\gamma$: in any local tangent frame expand $V=\sum_av^ae_a(\gamma)$ and apply [F5] and the ordinary product rule to each ambient component. This derives the formula for arbitrary along-curve fields, without requiring an ambient extension of $V$. On the equator, $T'= -\gamma$ and $\langle\dot\gamma,Tangle=1$, so $D_t^{
abla}T=0$. Also $N'=0$ and $\langle\dot\gamma,Nangle=0$, so $D_t^{
abla}N=0$.
